===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|status|lang=enm}} < {{etyl|fro}} {{term|status|lang=fro}} < {{etyl|LL.}} {{term|statutum||a statute}}, neuter singular of {{etyl|la}} {{term|statutus}}, past participle of {{term|statuere||to set up, establish}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈstætʃuːt/}}, {{SAMPA|/"st{tSu:t/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Written law, as laid down by the [[legislature]].
# {{legal}} (Common law) Legislated rule of [[society]] which has been given the force of law by those it governs.

